# trivyignore-template: v1 — ships WITH .github/workflows/nightly.yml, whose
# trivy job passes `--ignorefile .trivyignore`. Trivy treats a MISSING ignore
# file as a FATAL flag error, not an empty list, so a repo that copies the
# workflow without this file has a Trivy job that has NEVER SCANNED ANYTHING —
# red on a flag error, with its real findings hidden behind it (measured:
# go-enclave 2026-08-26, ten HIGH x/crypto CVEs sat behind the FATAL for the
# workflow's whole life; go-enclave PR #5).
#
# Source of truth: software/templates/github-actions/.trivyignore in the
# automatethethings repo. Keep this EMPTY except for CVE IDs with a dated
# reason:
#
#   # 2026-01-01 <who>: <why this finding does not apply here>
#   CVE-XXXX-NNNNN
